1
00:00:00,320 --> 00:00:02,400
An auditor ticks one box for this setting.

2
00:00:02,400 --> 00:00:03,599
There are two.

3
00:00:04,554 --> 00:00:06,513
This is the Copilot settings blade.

4
00:00:06,513 --> 00:00:09,474
One entry, screen and camera sharing.

5
00:00:10,444 --> 00:00:12,884
It opens into two controls, not one.

6
00:00:13,838 --> 00:00:14,638
Screens.

7
00:00:14,638 --> 00:00:15,638
Cameras.

8
00:00:15,638 --> 00:00:18,358
One row, two values behind it.

9
00:00:19,320 --> 00:00:23,520
Screens offers all users, no users, or specific groups.

10
00:00:24,720 --> 00:00:25,800
So does Cameras.

11
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:26,880
Independently.

12
00:00:29,350 --> 00:00:32,629
Nothing was changed to film this, which is why Save is greyed.

13
00:00:35,084 --> 00:00:38,084
Turn screens off and you have done half the job.

14
00:00:38,084 --> 00:00:40,844
The camera is still on, and your note says handled.

15
00:00:41,814 --> 00:00:45,014
An audit note that records one value carries neither.

16
00:00:45,014 --> 00:00:50,254
Write down two, one per control, and check Save is greyed before you record either.

17
00:00:51,208 --> 00:00:57,088
The Copilot Hardening Baseline walks the Copilot settings blade one entry at a time, this one included.

18
00:00:57,088 --> 00:00:58,088
Link below.

